My main beef with pudding farming, and item creation on monster death in
general, is that it's counter intuitive behaviour even by NetHack
standards.  Whacking an animate pudding with a rusty dagger and having it
divide in two I have no problem with, and seems to me to be a relatively
"non-magical" event.  Having monsters occasionally materialize "out of thin
air" is a little more of a stretch, but I can also deal with it, especially
since their are obvious game-play enhancing reasons for it to occur.

On the other hand, having items mysteriously appear out of thin air
whenever a monster dies bothers me, and goes beyond my suspension of
disbelief, especially since there are no particularly convincing
game-enhancing reasons to do so.  Why can't monsters' inventory be
generated with the monster, instead of when the monster dies?

